	I have been playing hack since Don Kneller ported it to the PC 
and have read this newsgroup since that time.  As most people that post here
I have my share of gripes and ideas about the game.  I'll save the gripes
for another post, but I can't hold in the ideas any longer...


This is my nethack wish list...


	1.  I always thought that there should be a bag of some kind
for carrying things...(bag of holding) I was thinking of a more specific
type of bag like a gem sack.  Would turn gems to rocks if cursed, glass
to gems if blessed stuff like that.  No big deal.

	2.  One thing I would like to see is a henchman.  He could carry
some stuff for you but would not use it.  He would have minimal armor and
weapons and little, if any, intelligence and wisdom.  He would kill only 
for food.  Could use commands like #give and #get for transferring goods
to and from him.
	The henchman could also be more of an active player in the sense
that he could do things like map out part of the dungeon for you.  He 
could also let you know of things like shops, zoos, undead rooms... by 
wandering around the dungeon on his own.  The activeness of the 
henchman could be different depending on his intelligence or wisdom or
something (phase of the moon, high tide in Hawaii, etc...).
 
	3.  I would like to see more creative dungeon levels.  This is not
a major thing but it would make things more interesting. Some suggestions: 

- A level with one big room in the middle and a bunch of little rooms(closets)
branching off from the big room. Both up and down stairs would be in the
big room and some of the little rooms could have ladders up to small lofts.
The big room could have a river or stream running through it that would
require a raft to cross (or a bridge).

- A level that would have a couple of rooms on one side and a small 'magic
maze' on the other.  the maze would have some one-way doors, looping halls,
various traps and other such goodies.  Maybe the walls could be undiggable.
No teleporting out either.  The maze could lead to some kind of treasure
room or dragon lair.

- How about a room that is like a treasure room with a few chests and things,
that have stone guards on both sides of the doorway that would come to life
if you try to leave.  Likewise there could be force fields preventing you 
from leaving the room.  Maybe a secret switch could deactivate the fields.

	4.  I know some people are going to bitch and moan about this one
but I think it would be a good good idea to have a chainsaw.  This could
bring about a whole new set of tools: chainsaw chain, oil can(for oiling the
chain), gas can, spark plug, etc...  This would be a vicious weapon and 
would add a number of effects: attack monster(as usual), chain 
breaks (injuring you), you would need to start the saw, it would break down
and need repair(chainsaw shop), run out of fuel, etc...  You could even
add diamonds to the chain for digging.  Go ahead flamers...

	5.  This one is from my girlfriend(who also plays), Lederhosen.
these could be worn under armor and would protect against cold. Other items:
scroll of wishing(one wish), maybe a weapon (or wand) that reduces armor class, 
a torch, book of matches, etc...  Another thing, how about slapping a gem
of some kind on the end of a wand to disperse the ray in a wider path.


	O.K., I've got a bunch more, but the flame captains will have a 
field day on these alone so I'll hold them for later... 

Just my 2 cents worth...

T.R. Garman


